{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review

    One enrolment application, read as a decision funnel, with the controls to decide it.

    The reading order is the order of the decider's questions: the strip (who, in what state, how
    and through which method), what weighs on the decision, what confirming does with the
    adjustments folded under it, the message and the note, then the decision bar. The evidence -
    comment, submitted details, earlier applications - is a quieter column after the funnel in
    source order, beside it on wide screens and below it on narrow ones, reached through the
    signals' links. Focus order follows source order.

    The form posts the queue's own contract - a formaction naming the decision, a non-empty
    userenrolments array and the session key - so every guard manage.php applies to a queue
    decision applies here too; the only extra branch is the confirmation manage.php asks for
    before a cancel from this page. The application id travels in a hidden input rather than a
    checkbox because there is only ever one, and each decision is a submit button carrying its
    own formaction value, so the button pressed is the decision taken.

    Values arrive in their plain spelling and are output through double stashes, which escape
    each exactly once. The triple-stashed exceptions each say why in the partial that holds them.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * candecide boolean - whether this reader may decide the application. False for a holder of
      enrol/apply:viewapplications alone: the funnel renders without the outcome, the form, the
      controls and the sticky footer
    * viewonlynotice string - what a reader who may not decide is told above the funnel
    * formurl string - url the decision form posts back to
    * sesskey string - session key guarding the state change
    * userenrolmentid int - the application being decided
    * actions array - the three decisions, each with value, label and consequence (ESCAPED, hence
      the triple stash); listed here again, in the page body, for narrow screens where the bar
      has room for the buttons alone. aria-hidden, because each button's aria-describedby points
      at its own line in the bar (enrol_apply/review_actions)
    * stickyfooter string - the three decisions, already rendered into a core sticky footer by
      the renderer and interpolated INSIDE this form. The footer is never moved in the DOM -
      its placement is CSS - so the submits inside it post with the rest of the form, exactly as
      the queue's own bar does
    * everything enrol_apply/review_summary, enrol_apply/review_signals,
      enrol_apply/review_outcome and enrol_apply/review_evidence require

    Example context (json):
    {
        "candecide": true,
        "viewonlynotice": "You can view this application but not decide it.",
        "formurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?userenrol=42",
        "sesskey": "Ab12Cd34Ef",
        "userenrolmentid": 42,
        "status": "Awaiting a decision",
        "statuslabel": "Status",
        "statuschipclass": "bg-warning text-dark",
        "methodlabel": "Method",
        "methodname": "Application with a group key",
        "courselabel": "Course",
        "coursename": "R&D < Team induction",
        "courseurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=7",
        "profileurl": "https://example.com/user/view.php?id=5&course=7",
        "profilelabel": "View profile",
        "signalsheading": "What weighs on the decision",
        "attention": "Nothing is over a limit. The decision is still yours.",
        "signals": [
            {"label": "No comment from the applicant", "isnone": true}
        ],
        "outcomeheading": "On confirming",
        "outcomesentence": "Ana Souza joins the course as Student, without a group, and is notified of the approval.",
        "writelabel": "Write to the applicant or add a note for the record",
        "messagelabel": "Message to the applicant",
        "notelabel": "Note for the record",
        "commentlabel": "Comment",
        "nocomment": "The applicant did not write anything.",
        "actions": [
            {"value": "cancel", "label": "Cancel this application", "consequence": "Ends the application"},
            {"value": "confirm", "label": "Confirm this application", "consequence": "Joins the course"}
        ],
        "stickyfooter": "<div id=\"sticky-footer\"><button type=\"submit\">Confirm</button></div>"
    }
}}
{{!
    The decision form wraps the funnel only for a reader who may decide. A viewer reads the same
    blocks inside a plain container instead, so the opening and closing tags are chosen twice, by
    the same flag; each rendering is balanced.
}}
{{#candecide}}
<form id="enrol_apply_review_form" class="enrol_apply-review" method="post" action="{{formurl}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="userenrolments[]" value="{{userenrolmentid}}">
{{/candecide}}
{{^candecide}}
<div class="enrol_apply-review">
    <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">{{viewonlynotice}}</div>
{{/candecide}}
    {{> enrol_apply/review_summary }}
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-8 enrol_apply-reviewfunnel">
            {{> enrol_apply/review_signals }}
            {{#candecide}}
                {{> enrol_apply/review_outcome }}
            {{/candecide}}
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-4 enrol_apply-reviewevidence">
            {{> enrol_apply/review_evidence }}
        </div>
    </div>
{{#candecide}}
    <ul class="enrol_apply-consequences list-unstyled small d-md-none" aria-hidden="true">
        {{#actions}}
            <li>{{label}}: <span data-region="consequence-{{value}}">{{{consequence}}}</span></li>
        {{/actions}}
    </ul>
    {{{stickyfooter}}}
</form>
{{/candecide}}
{{^candecide}}
</div>
{{/candecide}}
